ore recording an album. The group released their album [i]Jade to the Max[/i] in 1992, which spawned the top-charting singles \"I Wanna Love You\", \"Don't Walk Away\", and \"One Woman\". Their second album [i]Mind, Body & Song[/i], released in 1994, produced another top-charting single \"Every Day of the Week\".\n\nThe group disbanded in late 1995 but reformed as a duo in 1997 with Joi Marshall and Tonya Kelly, who released a single \"Keep on Rising\". In 2014, they resurfaced again, without Reed, and released another single \"Baby Luv\", which featured vocalist Myracle Holloway. Although the original members planned to reunite in 2019, those plans failed to materialize when Marshall and Kelly toured with Myracle Holloway as their new member and refused to include Reed.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:139169","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":[{"active":false,"id":338016,"name":"Angela Slates"},{"active":false,"id":935499,"name":"Di Reed"},{"active":true,"id":935501,"name":"Joi Marshall"},{"active":true,"id":935502,"name":"Tonya Kelly"},{"active":false,"id":3212081,"name":"Debbie Mitchell"},{"active":true,"id":6738782,"name":"Myracle Holloway"}],"namevariations":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/139169-Jade-3","type":"artist","urls":["https://www.officialjademusic.com/","https://www.instagram.com/ladiesofjade/"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/15261/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"15261","image":"https://i.discogs.com/Yl3_1-BA--jHCayImBXIoKi9-gBYcxp0NHkWBzNZe3I/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:432/w:380/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTE1MjYx/LTE1MTE4MDEzNjEt/NTk2Ni5qcGVn.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/amBeiYXuPD_Nto3mvWt_PAnDM0xYy6NtD2NYrk28is8/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTE1MjYx/LTE1MTE4MDEzNjEt/NTk2Ni5qcGVn.jpeg","profile":"American soul and R&B singer and musician, born 24 January 1941 in New Orleans, Louisiana, USA. Father of [a=Ivan Neville] and