"discogs:label:3791666","relations":{"parentLabel":{"id":3791660,"name":"Bleach Bros. Music Group"},"sublabels":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/label/3791666-BBMG","type":"label","urls":[]}},"/api/discogs/label/602460/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"602460","image":"https://i.discogs.com/IWXchVPn3kqV5cHC1eov55GfDOQOrJxd2AvGROXB45Y/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTYwMjQ2/MC0xNjI5MTk1OTYx/LTI3NDcuanBlZw.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/HT0YuqpcQ0aSZ_8FPX5laGg7z7p0y26e_YZQMNV2Jj4/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTYwMjQ2/MC0xNjI5MTk1OTYx/LTI3NDcuanBlZw.jpeg","profile":"Die Orakel (Engl. the oracles) might not know it all but has the capacity to observe and sense it: Oliver Hafenbauer’s imprint operates as an experimental field for electronic music on the playfully indecisive end where it exceeds genre-specificity to focus on tunes that function beyond. This is not to say that there are no four-to-the-floor productions. The Frankfurt-based label features contributions by artists like upsammy, Edward, Roman Flügel or Poly Chain, all known as dance floor doyens. The releases yet encompass what can slip the attention on a traditional dance label.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:label:602460","relations":{"parentLabel":null,"sublabels":[{"id":2022990,"name":"ORKL-0114-Series"}]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/label/602460-Die-Orakel","type":"label","urls":["https://dieorakel.bandcamp.com","https://soundcloud.com/die-orakel","https://www.facebook.com/dieorakel","https://www.instagram.com/dieorakel/","https://www.youtube.com/Orakelkanal"]}},"/api/discogs/label/90091/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"90091","image":"https://i.discogs.com/1-khFGQVYzHSy9mRF266b6ashpjLwglqto52yBOpGyI/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTkwMDkx/LTE3NTExMDQ2NTIt/NjAwMC5wbmc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/7CPoyimBTqtkkFR1AL70JPqYPEaOZvPq-WJd576BFu0/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTkwMDkx/LTE3NTExMDQ2NTIt/NjAwMC5wbmc.jpeg","profile":"Multinational label.\r\nLabel Code: LC 2822 / LC 02822\r\nThe [l=Warner Classics] imprint originated from the old [l=Warner Classics International] division of the [l=Warner Music Group], before reorganization within the group made it part of [l=Warner Music UK Ltd.]. For a few years in the late 2000s, [l=Warner Classics] and [l=Warner Jazz] were merged to form [l=Warner Classics & Jazz]. \r\nIn 2012, Universal Music Group (UMG) bought [l=EMI]. Approval of the merger by the EU (in 2013) required that the combined company divest itself “of one third of its total operations to other companies with a proven track record in the music industry.” (Wikipedia)\r\nIn 2014 Warner Classics absorbed [l=EMI Classics] and [l=Virgin Classics], as well as reviving the [l=Erato] label. Warner Classics moved its headquarters to Paris as part of the Classics division reorganization under [l= Parlophone Records Ltd.].\r\n\r\nWhile Warner Music Group owns the former EMI and Virgin Classics catalogs, UMG retains the EMI and Virgin trademarks.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:label:90091","relations":{"parentLabel":{"id":22328,"name":"Warner Music UK Ltd."},"sublabels":[{"id":362441,"name":"100 Best"},{"id":1466376,"name":"5 Classic Albums (4)"},{"id":1871569,"name":"50 Best"},{"id":1620006,"name":"Artist Portrait"},{"id":4287283,"name":"Bruckner 200"},{"id":1381436,"name":"Callas Live Remastered"},{"id":742108,"name":"Callas Remastered"},{"id":2657992,"name":"Calm (2)"},{"id":2601289,"name":"Classic Masters (4)"},{"id":489321,"name":"Collector's Edition (3)"},{"id":1063558,"name":"Cologne Collection"},{"id":34406,"name":"EMI Classics"},{"id":1879333,"name":"Essential Classics (4)"},{"id":317984,"name":"Gemini (9)"},{"id":689887,"name":"Inspiration"},{"id":1381652,"name":"Karajan Official Remastered Edition